            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous coronary intervention for extrinsic coronary compression after pulmonary valve replacement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>482-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery compression is a rare and potentially fatal complication after pulmonary valve replacement. This report describes myocardial infarction from extrinsic left main coronary artery compression after pulmonary valve replacement in a 10-y-old boy. He was successfully treated with percutaneous coronary intervention.</AbstractText>
